# Steps to install SASS using npm

1. Make sure Node.js and npm are installed.
   You can verify this by running:
   node -v
   npm -v

2. Open a terminal (Command Prompt, Git Bash, or PowerShell).

3. If using PowerShell and encountering script execution errors, run:
   Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass

4. Run the following command to install a specific version of SASS:
   npm install sass@3.7.4

5. Verify installation:
   npx sass --version
